                                                                   Job roles, teams, groups and companies

1. Job role

A job role is the type of work a person does. It is a label like Designer or QA Tester.
Why it matters:
A project manager can assign a task to the role Designer instead of to a specific person, and decide who does it later.
It helps with planning. If a project needs 3 designers and you only have 2, the role shows the gap.

2.Team

A team is a set of people who work together on the same work, for example the “Website Team.”
Why it matters:
You can assign a task to the whole team, and anyone on the team can pick it up.
A team can have its own request queue or its own view of the team’s work.

Remember: A team is about working together. A person can be on several teams.

3. Group
It represents a unit in your company’s organizational structure.Its job is to place every user and many other objects somewhere in the company hierarchy.

Sharing. You can share an object (a report, dashboard, project, template and so on) with a group, and the members of that group get the access you set. This avoids adding people one at a time.
Reports and filters. Because every user sits in one home group, you can filter and group data by department, like “hours logged by Marketing” or “projects owned by IT.”
Assigning objects to a group. Objects such as projects can also carry a group, which lets you report on work by department.
Why it matters:
Groups are used for sharing and permissions. You can share a report or project with a whole group in one step.
They are also used for reporting, such as hours by department.

Remember: A group is about where someone sits in the organization, and a team is about who they work with. They can be different. Someone from the IT group may sit on the Website Team.


4. Company
A company is the organization a user, project or object belongs to. If your business works for clients, each client can be a company, and the projects for them are linked to it. Your own organization is also a company.
Why it matters: It lets you separate and report by organization, for example “show me all projects for Acme Foods.”

Interview questions
. What is the difference between a team and a group?
A team is people who work together on the same work, like the “Website Team.” You can give a task to the whole team. 
A user can be on many teams, and a team has many users. (many-to-many)

Group:
A Group is an organizational structure in Workfront used to manage users and apply group-level settings and preferences.
Groups are mainly used for sharing and reports.A user has one home group. One group has many users. (one-to-many)	


